<title>GERMANY: Waigel-Germany can reach EMU goal if jobless falls.</title>
<headline>Waigel-Germany can reach EMU goal if jobless falls.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German finance minister Theo Waigel said on Saturday that he believed Germany could meet single European currency criteria on government deficits if unemployment fell as forecast.  </p>
<p>Waigel was speaking at a breakfast briefing for journalists ahead of Saturday's G7 summit of finance ministers and central bank chiefs.</p>
<p>His comments follow widespread concern that Germany could fail to reach the 3.0 percent deficit-to-gross domestic product criteria set out in the Maastricht Treaty for entry into the single European currency after posting record high unemployment in January.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
